# Expected outcomes where Wycheproof's own verdict does not decide: every "acceptable" vector,
# and every known deviation from a "valid" or "invalid" verdict. Reviewed by hand; the reason is
# part of the line. Format (see conformance.py):
#
#   <vector file> tc=<id>|flag=<name> accept|reject <reason>
#
# A tc= line wins over flag= lines; among flag= lines the first one in this file that names one
# of the vector's flags wins, so the stricter rule comes first. "accept" means the call succeeded
# and gave the vector's output. A line that no vector uses fails the run, so this file cannot go
# stale: when a bump changes a behaviour, the line has to be looked at again.
# This is the file for the ESP-IDF 6 pins (PINS.idf6, CRYPTO_EXPECTATIONS): each line below was
# checked again against mbedTLS 4.1.1, not copied. Paths are mbedTLS's at MBEDTLS_COMMIT
# (ce3f3485, mbedTLS 4.1.1): library/ for X.509 and TLS; the crypto has moved to TF-PSA-Crypto,
# so "ecp.c", "rsa.c" and "psa_crypto_ecp.c" are tf-psa-crypto/drivers/builtin/src/,
# "asn1parse.c" tf-psa-crypto/utilities/, "psa_util.c" tf-psa-crypto/core/ and "pk_wrap.c"
# tf-psa-crypto/extras/. tls_engine.c is this tree's software/wifi/raw_u64/main/tls_engine.c.

# ---- X25519 (RFC 7748) ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# A low-order public key gives an all-zero shared secret. RFC 8446 7.4.2 says a TLS 1.3 client
# MUST abort on it. mbedTLS 4.1.1 refuses it once, on the input: PSA's ECDH loads the peer's key
# through mbedtls_ecp_check_pubkey() (psa_crypto_ecp.c:174-175), which refuses the known low-order
# u values (ecp.c:2792-2842: 0, 1, p-1, and Curve25519's two others). That list is the only
# barrier. 3.6 had two more: its ladder's Z = 0 had no inverse, but 4.1.1's inversion
# (MPI_ECP_INV, ecp.c:1129-1130, mbedtls_mpi_gcd_modinv_odd()) returns success with an
# indeterminate result when there is none (conf4-adversarial1 M4, measured); and ecdh.c's check
# of the result is gone, PSA's ECDH writing the secret out as it is (psa_crypto_ecp.c:522-536).
x25519_test.json flag=ZeroSharedSecret reject all-zero shared secret refused: the low-order u values are refused on input (ecp.c:2792-2842), as RFC 8446 7.4.2 requires of TLS 1.3
# RFC 7748 section 5 defines X25519 for every 32-byte u: points on the twist, u >= p (taken
# mod p) and the special values are all inputs the function must compute on. mbedTLS does,
# with the right result (an "accept" is checked against Wycheproof's shared secret).
x25519_test.json flag=Twist accept RFC 7748 5: X25519 is defined on twist points; computed correctly
x25519_test.json flag=NonCanonicalPublic accept RFC 7748 5: u >= 2^255-19 is reduced mod p; computed correctly
x25519_test.json flag=SpecialPublicKey accept RFC 7748 5: special u values are ordinary inputs; computed correctly

# ---- X448 (RFC 7748; offered by mbedTLS 4's defaults, group 001e) ---------------------------
# The same single barrier as X25519 (ecp.c:2792-2842 refuses u = 0, 1 and p-1 for Curve448), and
# the same RFC 7748 section 5 rules for the rest.
# A public key longer than the curve's 56 bytes is not an X448 key; PSA refuses it by its size
# (psa_crypto_ecp.c:124-128). Listed only because the SpecialPublicKey line would claim these.
x448_test.json flag=PublicKeyTooLong reject a key of the wrong length is refused (psa_crypto_ecp.c:124-128), as Wycheproof wants
x448_test.json flag=ZeroSharedSecret reject all-zero shared secret refused: the low-order u values are refused on input (ecp.c:2792-2842), as RFC 8446 7.4.2 requires of TLS 1.3
x448_test.json flag=Twist accept RFC 7748 5: X448 is defined on twist points; computed correctly
x448_test.json flag=NonCanonicalPublic accept RFC 7748 5: u >= p is reduced mod p; computed correctly
x448_test.json flag=SpecialPublicKey accept RFC 7748 5: special u values are ordinary inputs; computed correctly

# ---- ECDH on the NIST curves (key_share) ---------------------------------------------------
# TLS 1.3 only allows the uncompressed point format (RFC 8446 4.2.8.2), and PSA's raw key
# agreement only takes that format: a Weierstrass public key must be 2m+1 bytes
# (psa_crypto_ecp.c:104-115), so a compressed one has the wrong size for the curve (:124-128).
ecdh_secp256r1_ecpoint_test.json flag=CompressedPublic reject compressed points are not allowed in a TLS 1.3 key_share (RFC 8446 4.2.8.2)
ecdh_secp384r1_ecpoint_test.json flag=CompressedPublic reject compressed points are not allowed in a TLS 1.3 key_share (RFC 8446 4.2.8.2)
ecdh_secp521r1_ecpoint_test.json flag=CompressedPublic reject compressed points are not allowed in a TLS 1.3 key_share (RFC 8446 4.2.8.2)

