# ---- ECDSA: a known deviation, BER lengths instead of DER ----------------------------------
# Wycheproof calls these "invalid"; mbedTLS accepts them. Each is a correct signature (r and s
# have the right values) with long-form or zero-padded lengths: the pk layer turns the DER
# signature into PSA's raw r||s with mbedtls_ecdsa_der_to_raw() (pk_wrap.c:187), which reads
# the SEQUENCE and each INTEGER with mbedtls_asn1_get_tag() (psa_util.c:259, :199), and
# mbedtls_asn1_get_len() takes any length of 1 to 4 bytes (asn1parse.c:36-52). The effect is
# signature malleability: one signature has more than one byte string. It is not a forgery, and
# TLS 1.3 does not rely on signatures being unique. Unlike 3.6 (which read each INTEGER as an
# unsigned magnitude), 4.1.1 refuses an INTEGER that lacks its sign byte or has more than one
# leading zero (psa_util.c:205-222), so those vectors now get Wycheproof's own verdict. Every
# other encoding error Wycheproof tries (garbage, wrong tags, truncation, ...) is refused, which
# the run checks.
ecdsa_secp256r1_sha256_test.json flag=BerEncodedSignature accept deviation: BER lengths accepted (asn1parse.c:36-52); malleability, not forgery
ecdsa_secp256r1_sha512_test.json flag=BerEncodedSignature accept deviation: BER lengths accepted (asn1parse.c:36-52); malleability, not forgery
ecdsa_secp384r1_sha256_test.json flag=BerEncodedSignature accept deviation: BER lengths accepted (asn1parse.c:36-52); malleability, not forgery
ecdsa_secp384r1_sha384_test.json flag=BerEncodedSignature accept deviation: BER lengths accepted (asn1parse.c:36-52); malleability, not forgery
ecdsa_secp384r1_sha512_test.json flag=BerEncodedSignature accept deviation: BER lengths accepted (asn1parse.c:36-52); malleability, not forgery
ecdsa_secp521r1_sha512_test.json flag=BerEncodedSignature accept deviation: BER lengths accepted (asn1parse.c:36-52); malleability, not forgery
# The one BER form mbedTLS refuses: an indefinite length (asn1parse.c:40, a length byte of 0x80).
# Listed only because the BerEncodedSignature lines above would otherwise claim it.
ecdsa_secp256r1_sha256_test.json tc=48 reject indefinite length refused (asn1parse.c:40), as Wycheproof wants
ecdsa_secp256r1_sha512_test.json tc=48 reject indefinite length refused (asn1parse.c:40), as Wycheproof wants
ecdsa_secp384r1_sha256_test.json tc=48 reject indefinite length refused (asn1parse.c:40), as Wycheproof wants
