# ---- X.509 path validation (x509-limbo, SERVER cases) --------------------------------------
# Paths here are mbedTLS's library/ at MBEDTLS_COMMIT (4.1.1), and software/wifi/raw_u64/main/
# for tls_engine.c. In 4.1.1 the TLS 1.3 client checks a server certificate in
# mbedtls_ssl_verify_certificate() (ssl_tls.c), shared with TLS 1.2. "fail-closed" lines are valid chains mbedTLS refuses: an availability cost, not
# a security one. "DEVIATION" lines are chains limbo wants refused that mbedTLS accepts.
# limbo.c presents the intermediates in server order (on a path to a trusted certificate; every
# such path is tried), so these lines describe what mbedTLS does with a chain a server sends.
# What it does with a chain out of order is in the x509-misordered section below.
#
# Name constraints: mbedTLS 4.1.1, like 3.6, has no nameConstraints support, and a critical nameConstraints
# is an unknown critical extension, so any case with one in its certificates is refused at parse
# time, valid or not (781 valid BetterTLS cases, and the rfc5280::nc ones listed below).
limbo.json flag=critical-nameConstraints reject fail-closed: no nameConstraints support; a critical one is an unknown critical extension, so the certificate does not parse (x509_crt.c:949-956)
limbo.json tc=pathlen::validation-ignores-pathlen-in-leaf reject fail-closed (TLS 1.3): the leaf here has no digitalSignature keyUsage, which the TLS 1.3 client requires of a server certificate (ssl_tls.c:8848, mbedtls_ssl_check_cert_usage() at ssl_tls.c:8645-8713)
limbo.json tc=pathlen::self-issued-certs-pathlen reject fail-closed: mbedTLS counts this chain against the pathLenConstraint more strictly than RFC 5280 6.1.4(l)-(m)
limbo.json tc=pathlen::max-chain-depth-0-exhausted accept not a setting mbedTLS has: max_chain_depth is limbo's verifier parameter; mbedTLS has only the build-time MBEDTLS_X509_MAX_INTERMEDIATE_CA (8)
limbo.json tc=pathlen::max-chain-depth-1-exhausted accept not a setting mbedTLS has: max_chain_depth is limbo's verifier parameter; mbedTLS has only the build-time MBEDTLS_X509_MAX_INTERMEDIATE_CA (8)
limbo.json tc=rfc5280::aki::critical-aki accept DEVIATION (profile rule, not a path-validation step of RFC 5280 6.1): mbedTLS does not police how a CA encoded this certificate
limbo.json tc=rfc5280::aki::leaf-missing-aki accept DEVIATION (profile rule, not a path-validation step of RFC 5280 6.1): mbedTLS does not police how a CA encoded this certificate
limbo.json tc=rfc5280::aki::intermediate-missing-aki accept DEVIATION (profile rule, not a path-validation step of RFC 5280 6.1): mbedTLS does not police how a CA encoded this certificate
limbo.json tc=rfc5280::aki::cross-signed-root-missing-aki accept DEVIATION (profile rule, not a path-validation step of RFC 5280 6.1): mbedTLS does not police how a CA encoded this certificate
limbo.json tc=rfc5280::nc::permitted-dns-match reject fail-closed: no nameConstraints support; a critical one is an unknown critical extension, so the certificate does not parse (x509_crt.c:949-956)
limbo.json tc=rfc5280::nc::permitted-dns-match-noncritical accept fail-open:noncritical-nameconstraints DEVIATION: a non-critical nameConstraints is skipped unread (x509_crt.c:949-950), so it constrains nothing
limbo.json tc=rfc5280::nc::permitted-dns-match-more reject fail-closed: no nameConstraints support; a critical one is an unknown critical extension, so the certificate does not parse (x509_crt.c:949-956)
limbo.json tc=rfc5280::nc::permitted-ipv4-match reject fail-closed: no nameConstraints support; a critical one is an unknown critical extension, so the certificate does not parse (x509_crt.c:949-956)
